 "notes": "Spine: need -> gap (epoxy/silicone incompatibility) -> SER bridge hypothesis -> PSi + 18 wt% SER -> APTES prepolymerisation -> RTV coating -> ring-opened SER -> bonded network (argued) -> two branches: adhesion -> immersion performance, and N2 thermal stability -> 300 C air heat resistance -> conclusion. The bonded network is never measured on the cured coating (q18 basis argued, supported only by SEM compatibility). Air heat test (q28) inverts the N2 TGA ranking: pure PSi keeps more mass and colour; contrasts edge to q25. DTG (F10b) does not show a 95 C Tmax gain for S2-S4 (q24). F9 photos do not support 'S2 and S3 consistent' (q32). Storability (q13) is a property of the intermediate prepolymer, typed PRP/value with object=prepolymer. q9 fit poor: a partially weakened band sits between feature_presence and feature_quantification (see merge note). Figures opened: F5, F6, F9, F10. F4, F7, F8, F11, F12 not opened (text_only). Scheme 1-3 (F1-F3) not used."
